From 8efbe2776097ecfd0b7d7076acc625380a49887e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ashfordeOU <236818772+ashfordeOU@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 04:38:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] web: the IQ recording view in Kshana Desktop (studio/iq/),
 ported from the Studio source

A recording of any size read from disk in pieces through the app's read-only commands
(read_range, iq_probe): power and a waterfall over the whole file, the spectrum at a cursor,
played through. lib/iqview.mjs decodes ci8, cu8, ci16 and cf32, reads SigMF metadata and
computes a Hann-windowed Welch spectrum whose bins sum to the signal power. Read only: the
page has no control that writes a file, transmits or makes a signal. Outside the Desktop it
says it needs the Desktop; the tools hub links it from the IQ row in the Desktop only.

Ported from kshana-pro site/desktop-studio 71cac75; the site part is unchanged (8d10cf7).
port_site.py and site.test.mjs list studio/iq/index.html with the other Studio views;
i18n/en/studio-js.ftl regenerated with tools/i18n.mjs jsx (36 messages); a CI step runs
iqview.test.mjs.
